# <%= name %>

A Roblox game built with [KRF](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/) `<%= runtime.package %>@<%= runtime.version %>`.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run build
```

`npm install` installs [Rokit](https://github.com/rojo-rbx/rokit) if you don't have it, the Roblox
tools pinned in `rokit.toml`, and the Wally packages. Open `<%= name %>.rbxl` in Roblox Studio and press Play.
Hold F (or X on a gamepad) to Focus: Energy regenerates while you hold it.
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>

This is a Hybrid project: Rojo owns `src` and `Packages`, and your Studio place owns the world.
Save the built place somewhere else, keep building the world there, and sync code with `rojo serve`.
<% } -%>

## Scripts

| Script | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | Builds `<%= name %>.rbxl` |
| `npm run format` | Formats `src` |
| `npm run check` | Format check, lint and strict type check |

## Adding definitions

Add a ModuleScript anywhere under `src/server/Actions`, `Tags` or `Resources`; each folder's
`init.luau` loads every module beneath it. Actions return a factory function; Tags and Resources
return a definition table. Actions players request from the client also need an entry in
`src/shared/ActionRequests.luau` and a route in `src/client/Controls.luau`; held Actions also
need a `WhileDown` policy in `src/client/ActionInputPolicies.luau`.
